## Fix 3: Fix Refresh Token Cookie Path {#fix-3-fix-refresh-token-cookie-path}

**File:** `src/lib/auth.ts`

### Current Code (Line 140\-146) {#current-code-line-140-146}

```typescript
export const refreshCookieOptions = {
  httpOnly: true,
  secure: isProd,
  sameSite: "strict" as const,
  path: "/api/auth",  // ← TOO RESTRICTIVE
  maxAge: REFRESH_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS,
};
```

### Fixed Code {#fixed-code-1}

```typescript
export const refreshCookieOptions = {
  httpOnly: true,
  secure: isProd,
  sameSite: "strict" as const,
  path: "/",  // Allow from all paths (browser will still only send to /api/auth/refresh and parents)
  maxAge: REFRESH_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS,
};
```

**Why:** The browser automatically restricts cookie transmission based on request path matching. Setting `path: "/"` allows reading from any route while the browser still only sends the cookie to matching paths.

