## Fix 5: Verify & Fix TOTP Login Form UI {#fix-5-verify-fix-totp-login-form-ui}

**File:** `src/app/login/login-form.tsx`

### Checklist {#checklist}

- [ ] Login form has email \+ password fields (DONE)
- [ ] Form has CSRF token hidden field (DONE)
- [ ] Form has conditional TOTP input that shows when `needs2FA` is true (VERIFY)
- [ ] Form properly handles state transitions (initial login → TOTP input)
- [ ] TOTP field is cleared when switching back to password input

### Verification Points {#verification-points}

Look for in the login form:

```typescript
// 1. CSRF token field should exist
<input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value={csrfToken} />

// 2. TOTP input should be conditionally rendered
{needs2FA && (
  <input
    type="text"
    name="totp_code"
    placeholder="6-digit code"
    maxLength="6"
    pattern="\d{6}"
    required
  />
)}

// 3. Form action should handle both cases
const result = await loginAction(formData);
// Should show TOTP input if result.error === "2FA_REQUIRED"
```

If these are missing, add them. The form should:

1. Show email/password initially
2. On submit with valid creds, if 2FA required, show TOTP input
3. On TOTP submit, complete login

